The groups of dEQP-VK that Kosmos builds and runs (`docs/gpu3d.md` G2):
`info` and `api`. Under __kosmos__ the package registers those two, the
GLSL, Amber and experimental groups register nothing, and the module links
only the libraries the two are made of and the helpers the API tests
borrow from five other groups - so a group is added here, with its
library, when Kosmos runs it.

diff -ruN a/external/vulkancts/modules/vulkan/CMakeLists.txt b/external/vulkancts/modules/vulkan/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/external/vulkancts/modules/vulkan/CMakeLists.txt	2026-11-19 15:37:24.183421296 -0300
+++ b/external/vulkancts/modules/vulkan/CMakeLists.txt	2026-11-19 15:37:24.183602081 -0300
@@ -208,6 +208,27 @@
 	deqp-vk-video
 )
 
+# Kosmos's package is the groups vktTestPackage.cpp registers there, and
+# only their libraries are linked - with the helpers the API tests borrow
+# from other groups: image, Y'CbCr and pipeline's util libraries, Amber's,
+# and WSI's native objects, a library of one file so the WSI group itself
+# is not built.
+if (DEQP_TARGET STREQUAL "kosmos")
+	add_library(deqp-vk-wsi-native STATIC wsi/vktNativeObjectsUtil.cpp)
+	target_link_libraries(deqp-vk-wsi-native tcutil vkutil)
+	set(DEQP_VK_LIBS
+		tcutil
+		vkutil
+		deqp-vk-api
+		deqp-vk-image-util
+		deqp-vk-ycbcr-util
+		deqp-vk-pipeline-util
+		deqp-vk-amber
+		deqp-vk-wsi-native
+		deqp-vk-custom-instances-devices-util
+		)
+endif ()
+
 set(DEQP_VKSC_LIBS
 	tcutil
 	vkscutil
